Subject: [PATCH] Implement CSS counters: resolution pass + counter() content +
 markers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Counters simply didn't exist: pe_content_text handled a single literal
string and list markers came from a naive sibling index. Everything
else (counter()/counters()/attr() in generated content, counter-reset/
-increment/-set, ol[start]/ol[reversed]/li[value], reversed() auto
numbering) rendered as nothing or as the wrong number. The whole WPT
css-lists counter corpus failed on it.

layout/counters.rs adds a document-order pass (after styling, before
box construction) producing side tables: the list-item value per list
item and resolved ::before/::after content strings. Box construction
consumes them in pe_content_text_resolved and the marker builder;
markers gained decimal-leading-zero/lower- and upper-roman formatting.

The behavioural corners, each pinned by WPT css-lists:
- Scopes follow CSS 2.2 §12.4: creator + descendants + following
  siblings, sibling resets shadow at the same depth, implicitly
  created counters live at the root (counter-slot-order pins 1,2,3
  across slot boundaries), and traversal follows the flat tree.
- The HTML-implied list scope runs after the CSS resets so it beats
  the UA sheet's plain 'ol { counter-reset: list-item }', but yields
  to an author reversed()/non-zero reset (li-value-reversed-023).
- Element order is reset → increment (implicit list-item one included,
  even on li[value] items) → li[value] → counter-set
  (li-value-counter-reset-001 pins CSS counter-set beating value).
- reversed() auto-start = X − S: X is the first counter-set value in
  scope (or minus the last increment when there is none) and S the
  increment sum up to that set; plus one virtual increment when the
  setting element doesn't increment itself (li-value-reversed-019).
  Scanning covers pseudo-element declarations too.

css-lists reftests: 55/158 → 87/158. Not covered (pre-existing FAILs):
::marker content replacement, ::marker styling, and counter scoping
across shadow-boundary resets (counter-slot-order-scoping).

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: stylo 0.22 has no ContentItem::Attr;
attr() reaches the pass as a substituted String item.
